From 5e4fda66c4f0629a5a41a574d9c2102da106ac56 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ferdinand Vanmaele <ferdinand-joseph.vanmaele@uni-a.de>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 16:56:54 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 11/12] [clangd] workspace/symbol: abbreviated qualifiers on
 request (looseScope)

A client may send looseScope: true with workspace/symbol.  Then each
segment of the query's qualifier may fuzzy-match a segment of the
symbol's scope, in order, besides the exact sub-scope match: "geom::vert"
finds "dealii::GeometryInfo::vertices_per_cell", "tria::n_act"
"dealii::Triangulation::n_active_cells".  Off unless asked for; the
initialize reply announces workspaceSymbolMatchesProvider.looseScope, so
a client knows whether to ask.
